  "review": {
    "verdict": "PASS",
    "evidence": {
      "decisions_preserved": "PRD 'User flows and required behavior' preserves D1's Pi/Claude selection and 'complete source-relative path'; D2's regular, case-insensitive .md eligibility, unchanged disk and valid empty document; D3's current-content read on each explicit open; and D4's visible errors without absolute paths or stack traces. 'Scope and non-goals' preserves D5's read-only boundary.",
      "no_invention_or_contradiction": "No issues found. 'Constraints and dependencies' preserves C1–C2 and explicitly labels F1–F2 'observed, not requirements'; existing endpoint documentation and editing elsewhere are not promoted into scope. 'User flows and required behavior' retains A1's existing selection assumption and states 'no new navigation behavior is decided.' The opening note preserves the record's sanitized-fixture status rather than claiming new feature approval.",
      "scope_and_exclusions": "'Scope and non-goals' traces its open/display-or-error scope to SC1 and D5, explicitly retains all N1 exclusions, and preserves R1's rejection of autosave/editing. 'Constraints and dependencies' retains C1's localhost and existing fixture-root limits and C2's path validation, symlink exclusion and no-new-endpoint boundary.",
      "verifiable_acceptance": "'Vertical slices and observable acceptance criteria' retains AC1's displayed content and unchanged file bytes, AC2's uppercase-extension and empty-file success, AC3's current content after external modification, and AC4's errors for deleted/disallowed/unreadable targets without path or stack leakage or stale-document substitution. These provide observable success, freshness, read-only and failure checks consistent with D2–D4 and C2.",
      "useful_slices_and_dependencies": "'Vertical slices and observable acceptance criteria' explicitly states 'Slices are proposals, not approved requirements.' It preserves S1's valid-document read/display behavior across both sources, including empty and uppercase-extension files, linked to AC1–AC2. S2 retains its dependency on S1 and adds fresh reopen and safe failures linked to AC3–AC4.",
      "visible_unresolved_questions": "'Assumptions, open questions and deferred decisions' retains A1 and both unresolved questions: Q1's exact error and empty-view wording and Q2's rendering style, each labeled 'deferred, nonblocking.' Its statement 'content visibility only, not a new rendering engine' preserves Q2 and D5 without resolving deferred choices."
    },
